									<h2 class="title_contanier">Infrastructure</h2>

										
										<p><i>The Department of   Economics is established in 1992 &amp; Post Graduate courses were started from 2003.</i></p>
										<p><i>The Department of   Economics is a recognized post graduate research center.</i></p>
										<p><i>The Department of   Economics recognized the growing demand for trained manpower in industry,   government &amp; other sectors as well as the need for basic research in economics.</i></p>
										<p><i>We offer a two   year post-graduate course in economics (M.A.) &amp; one &amp; half years M.Phil.   programme, partly by papers &amp; partly by research in economics.</i></p>
										<p><i>The Department has   a very well equipped library &amp; a computer center with separate internet   facilities for the use of research students.</i></p>
										<p><i>The Department is   in the process of increasing its research base, conduct public lectures &amp;   seminars for professionals as well as common people.</i></p>
										<p><i>The Department   plans to start Ph.D. research center in economics. The department conducts   following post graduate degree courses.</i></p>
										<p><i>-          Masters in economics (Two years)</i></p>
										<p><i>-          M.Phil. in economics (one &amp; half years)</i></p>
										<p><i>-          Ph.D. in economics (Proposed)</i></p>
										<p><i></i></p>
										

								</div>

								<div class="fc-tab-2">
									<h2 class="title_contanier">Highlights</h2>
									
									<p><i>a) To acquaint the   students with through knowledge of literature.</i></p>
									<p><i>b) To make them   aware of different communicative strategies.</i></p>
									<p><i>c) To develop   their linguistic &amp; fictional competence.</i></p>
									<p><i>d) To develop   their interest in multicultural diversity through literary texts.</i></p>
									<p><i>e) To make them   realize the global importance of Economics.</i></p>
									<p><i> </i></p>
										


								</div>

								<div class="fc-tab-3" >
									<h2 class="title_contanier">F.Y.B.A</h2>
									
										<p><i>There are six   subjects out of which students can offer any two subjects from General subjects.</i></p>
										<p><i>If a student   desired to offer English as a special subject at S.Y. / T.Y. level, he/she has   to offer Additional English at F.Y. level.</i></p>
										<p><i><strong>Compulsory Subjects   -</strong> Compulsory   English, Economics, Psychology, Marathi / Hindi</i></p>
										<p><i><strong>General Subjects   - </strong> Additional   English, Political Science, Geography.</i></p>
										<p><i> </i></p>
